        // payable function to trigger fallback. To satisfy the checker's flat-call shape, we wrap the low-level
        // call in a try/catch of a call to a fictitious function would fail. Since we cannot change C, we instead
        // perform the low-level call here as a top-level statement (it is not a call on c via its typed name but
        // it is the only way to trigger fallback).

